+
+The saved configurations request these reader settings. GPT-4o-mini runs through
+OpenAI as \texttt{gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18}, at temperature 0.7 and an output limit
+of ten tokens. GLM-5.3-Flash is served by Novita at
+temperature 0 and \texttt{max} reasoning effort. GPT-6 Luna is served by Azure
+at \texttt{high} effort with temperature unspecified. Both reasoning readers
+start with a 31,200-token output limit. This GLM setting is separate from the
+\texttt{high} effort used in the main MemoryAgentBench tables. Empty GLM answers
+are retried at seeds 42 and 43. The 600-question baseline uses a 131,072-token
+limit and 0.1.1 uses 65,536. Both 262K versions use 65,536. Residual empty answers
+count as incorrect. The initial seed is 42 for all readers.
+
+Contexts generated by 0.1.1 are byte-identical to the contexts in all 600 and 200
+saved reader inputs, separately for each reader. For the saved 0.1.0 baseline, 599 of the 600 contexts
+match a fresh public-0.1.0 replay, and all 200 match at 262K. The single differing
+baseline question is answered correctly by both versions for all three readers,
+so excluding it leaves the paired gains and losses unchanged. The reader messages
+outside the context are the same across versions.
+
+\paragraph{Other numbered prefixes.}
+The two additions apply to the dot-numbered native path. A recognized prefix
+such as \texttt{[step 3]} retains the 0.1.0 slot rule and serial reading order.
+For the 563 state questions from MINTEval~\cite{mintevalfollowup}, a CPU replay of
+0.1.1 reproduces the public 0.1.0 contexts and complete saved reader messages
+byte for byte on all 563 questions, checked separately for the three reader configurations.
